1
00:00:32,870 --> 00:00:33,600
The Sun.

2
00:00:34,310 --> 00:00:36,060
A radiant happiness.

3
00:00:38,950 --> 00:00:41,420
You’re about to find happiness you’ve never known before.

4
00:00:43,070 --> 00:00:46,380
The sunlight will guide happiness into your life.

5
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:54,700
I have to say, your love life is especially blessed.

6
00:00:57,510 --> 00:01:03,340
Fate will lead you to love, but it's not always easy.

7
00:01:04,190 --> 00:01:05,099
But in the end,

8
00:01:05,830 --> 00:01:08,080
you’ll make it through just fine.

9
00:02:35,750 --> 00:02:37,050
What’s gotten into you two?

10
00:02:37,050 --> 00:02:38,590
One’s heart is burning with love,

11
00:02:38,590 --> 00:02:40,100
while the other’s hiding it deeply.

12
00:02:40,290 --> 00:02:41,829
Maybe Lord Sriprach

13
00:02:41,829 --> 00:02:45,630
has fallen for someone who’s already taken.

14
00:02:46,910 --> 00:02:47,820
Here’s your question.

15
00:02:47,820 --> 00:02:50,710
Do you like sneaking glances at me?

16
00:02:51,270 --> 00:02:52,980
You’ve fallen for someone, haven’t you?

17
00:02:53,460 --> 00:02:54,700
Do you really want to know?

18
00:02:55,100 --> 00:02:58,410
Then, go look into a looking glass,

19
00:02:58,410 --> 00:02:59,730
and you shall find the answer.

20
00:03:00,690 --> 00:03:03,780
Politics won’t be your downfall,

21
00:03:03,780 --> 00:03:04,930
but love will.

22
00:03:06,270 --> 00:03:07,520
Who exactly are you?

23
00:03:15,260 --> 00:03:16,060
I’m…

24
00:03:16,910 --> 00:03:17,620
Gaew.

25
00:03:18,820 --> 00:03:20,340
Your younger brother.

26
00:03:22,810 --> 00:03:23,450
No.

27
00:03:26,480 --> 00:03:29,630
Gaew doesn’t know other people’s fate.

28
00:03:31,510 --> 00:03:35,270
And he wouldn’t talk about parting as if he’s lived through it.

29
00:03:38,270 --> 00:03:40,730
If you’re bold enough to talk about my life,

30
00:03:41,570 --> 00:03:43,170
then you should be able to tell me.

31
00:03:45,150 --> 00:03:46,640
Where did you come from?

32
00:03:50,070 --> 00:03:51,020
Answer me.

33
00:03:53,770 --> 00:03:55,910
Are you really Gaew?

34
00:03:58,420 --> 00:04:00,020
Or someone else?

35
00:04:01,200 --> 00:04:02,350
Who are you, really?

36
00:04:16,970 --> 00:04:20,290
You can’t even answer such a simple question,

37
00:04:21,209 --> 00:04:23,370
so why should I listen to you,

38
00:04:24,500 --> 00:04:26,820
when you claim you can see my fate?

39
00:04:29,300 --> 00:04:31,360
Just trust me this once, P’Sri.

40
00:04:32,350 --> 00:04:34,850
If your concern is genuine,

41
00:04:35,980 --> 00:04:37,300
then I’m grateful.

42
00:04:40,090 --> 00:04:42,909
But you’ve never been in love.

43
00:04:44,560 --> 00:04:46,380
You don’t understand how I feel.

44
00:04:53,680 --> 00:04:55,040
Let me tell you this.

45
00:04:57,120 --> 00:04:59,230
You can stop many things,

46
00:05:01,030 --> 00:05:03,250
but stopping your heart is the hardest.

47
00:05:05,210 --> 00:05:07,420
And once you’ve fallen in love,

48
00:05:09,530 --> 00:05:10,690
even if you know it’s wrong,

49
00:05:13,510 --> 00:05:15,170
you still can’t stop loving them.

50
00:05:18,460 --> 00:05:20,590
Just give it some thought,

51
00:05:22,460 --> 00:05:23,150
P’Sri.

52
00:05:30,730 --> 00:05:32,150
Other than my fate,

53
00:05:33,590 --> 00:05:35,200
what else do you know?

54
00:05:36,720 --> 00:05:39,590
Tell me something else, and I might believe you.

55
00:05:41,590 --> 00:05:42,930
Even if I told you,

56
00:05:44,210 --> 00:05:45,920
you wouldn’t believe me anyway.

57
00:05:50,330 --> 00:05:51,630
Then predict something else.

58
00:05:53,909 --> 00:05:54,880
So…

59
00:05:56,880 --> 00:05:58,330
There will be political turmoil.

60
00:06:00,320 --> 00:06:02,110
A major conflict is coming.

61
00:06:06,700 --> 00:06:08,060
Who will start it?

62
00:06:10,100 --> 00:06:11,690
Who will be fighting whom?

63
00:06:13,030 --> 00:06:14,360
What will they be fighting over?

64
00:06:15,060 --> 00:06:16,100
When will it happen?

65
00:06:17,620 --> 00:06:20,100
You’re not serious, are you?

66
00:06:21,040 --> 00:06:22,140
I’m done talking.

67
00:06:23,270 --> 00:06:25,460
You’re saying it like there’s going to be a war.

68
00:06:26,790 --> 00:06:27,700
First,

69
00:06:28,150 --> 00:06:29,620
political turmoil

70
00:06:30,470 --> 00:06:31,550
will arise soon.

71
00:06:33,440 --> 00:06:34,430
As for war,

72
00:06:35,550 --> 00:06:37,170
it won’t happen anytime soon.

73
00:06:48,470 --> 00:06:49,250
Right now,

74
00:06:49,659 --> 00:06:52,820
Okya-Wichayen has grown obsessed with power.

75
00:06:53,530 --> 00:06:54,830
He fears no one.

76
00:06:55,750 --> 00:06:58,730
He even forced monks to leave the monkhood

77
00:06:58,730 --> 00:07:00,560
to help him build fortresses.

78
00:07:00,950 --> 00:07:04,000
And he surrounds himself with foreigners.

79
00:07:04,480 --> 00:07:08,080
This is overstepping the bounds of a nobleman.

80
00:07:09,100 --> 00:07:10,620
I’ve heard about this.

81
00:07:10,960 --> 00:07:12,700
Every town is living in fear.

82
00:07:12,950 --> 00:07:16,550
Some even sent tribute to the foreigners.

83
00:07:17,670 --> 00:07:18,510
What’s more,

84
00:07:18,870 --> 00:07:21,140
there are rumors that Phra Pi

85
00:07:21,750 --> 00:07:24,270
has converted to the foreigners’ religion.

86
00:07:24,820 --> 00:07:26,270
I’m afraid

87
00:07:27,060 --> 00:07:31,060
our kingdom may end up in the foreigners’ hands.

88
00:07:33,680 --> 00:07:35,250
I’m afraid so.

89
00:07:35,890 --> 00:07:38,880
If they decide to rebel,

90
00:07:40,470 --> 00:07:42,340
our kingdom will be engulfed in flames

91
00:07:43,430 --> 00:07:45,830
or cease to exist.

92
00:08:02,950 --> 00:08:03,600
Pin.

93
00:08:04,590 --> 00:08:05,360
Understood.

94
00:08:38,299 --> 00:08:40,289
I made your favorite dish.

95
00:09:04,310 --> 00:09:05,100
You…

96
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:08,070
never forget what I like.

97
00:09:09,990 --> 00:09:11,120
I appreciate it.

98
00:09:18,670 --> 00:09:19,520
My lord.

99
00:09:20,990 --> 00:09:22,080
Gaew is here to see you.

100
00:09:22,770 --> 00:09:23,440
Gaew.

101
00:09:31,600 --> 00:09:34,630
Can we talk for a moment?

102
00:09:35,630 --> 00:09:36,300
Of course.

103
00:09:38,330 --> 00:09:40,170
I always have time for my friend.

104
00:09:40,740 --> 00:09:41,470
Have a seat.

105
00:09:44,310 --> 00:09:46,660
If it’s something important, I’ll excuse myself.

106
00:09:46,970 --> 00:09:47,930
You don’t have to leave.

107
00:09:50,350 --> 00:09:52,060
You’re important to me.

108
00:09:52,800 --> 00:09:53,740
There’s nothing

109
00:09:54,400 --> 00:09:57,420
between us that you can’t know.

110
00:10:04,260 --> 00:10:06,370
I just want to say a few things,

111
00:10:07,110 --> 00:10:08,270
and then I’ll leave.

112
00:10:13,390 --> 00:10:15,310
I want to give you a sincere warning.

113
00:10:16,890 --> 00:10:18,590
What you’re doing

114
00:10:19,520 --> 00:10:20,610
is beyond your authority,

115
00:10:21,310 --> 00:10:22,690
and it’ll only bring you trouble.

116
00:10:27,860 --> 00:10:28,860
Let me be blunt.

117
00:10:30,160 --> 00:10:32,020
Don’t persuade Phra Pi to change his religion

118
00:10:32,850 --> 00:10:34,430
for your political gain.

119
00:10:49,200 --> 00:10:50,390
I want you

120
00:10:50,970 --> 00:10:52,810
to believe my warning above all else.

121
00:10:56,400 --> 00:10:57,230
Power,

122
00:10:57,980 --> 00:10:58,950
fame,

123
00:10:59,840 --> 00:11:00,820
and wealth

124
00:11:01,840 --> 00:11:03,090
are all temporary.

125
00:11:06,750 --> 00:11:07,570
I…

126
00:11:08,380 --> 00:11:09,410
hope you

127
00:11:10,210 --> 00:11:11,120
and Maria

128
00:11:14,790 --> 00:11:16,340
can build a family together

129
00:11:17,460 --> 00:11:18,890
and live a happy life.

130
00:11:20,540 --> 00:11:22,450
If those words

131
00:11:22,830 --> 00:11:25,700
hadn’t come from someone I consider a friend,

132
00:11:27,450 --> 00:11:30,080
I wouldn’t have listened in silence.

133
00:11:34,570 --> 00:11:35,890
I am the one

134
00:11:37,520 --> 00:11:39,860
who decides my own path.

135
00:11:42,480 --> 00:11:44,030
If anything happens,

136
00:11:45,110 --> 00:11:46,990
I’ll take responsibility.

137
00:11:48,300 --> 00:11:49,180
Gaew.

138
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:51,010
If so,

139
00:11:52,230 --> 00:11:54,230
then I have nothing more to say.

140
00:12:49,940 --> 00:12:50,900
Isn’t that Pin?

141
00:12:53,180 --> 00:12:54,400
P’Muen.

142
00:13:09,940 --> 00:13:10,980
Do you know

143
00:13:12,880 --> 00:13:15,450
how much this kingdom has done for us?

144
00:13:16,540 --> 00:13:18,180
It has never turned away...

145
00:13:18,180 --> 00:13:20,180
people of different races and faiths.

146
00:13:22,060 --> 00:13:24,010
Instead, it gave them shelter.

147
00:13:25,010 --> 00:13:26,070
As its people,

148
00:13:27,270 --> 00:13:29,360
we should be grateful,

149
00:13:30,450 --> 00:13:33,980
not think of harming this land.

150
00:13:43,150 --> 00:13:46,230
You make it sound like I’m betraying this country.

151
00:13:48,340 --> 00:13:50,140
I hope what I’ve said

152
00:13:52,370 --> 00:13:53,900
gives you something to think about.

153
00:13:55,040 --> 00:13:56,460
What you’re doing

154
00:13:57,200 --> 00:14:00,130
is sowing discord to the kingdom.

155
00:14:02,560 --> 00:14:04,710
You tricked Phra Pi into joining your side.

156
00:14:08,550 --> 00:14:10,300
You’ve talked too much.

157
00:14:11,650 --> 00:14:13,460
If you think I’m meddling,

158
00:14:14,490 --> 00:14:15,300
then…

159
00:14:16,310 --> 00:14:20,650
I hope you’re happy with your wealth

160
00:14:21,710 --> 00:14:22,980
all alone.

161
00:14:30,690 --> 00:14:31,420
Guyomar.

162
00:15:02,030 --> 00:15:02,790
Gaew.

163
00:15:05,310 --> 00:15:06,420
What did Pin tell you?

164
00:15:08,490 --> 00:15:10,030
If I hadn’t had Pin follow you,

165
00:15:10,820 --> 00:15:12,070
I never would’ve known

166
00:15:12,070 --> 00:15:13,920
you went to see Okya-Wichayen.

167
00:15:15,300 --> 00:15:17,820
What are you trying to say?

168
00:15:19,350 --> 00:15:20,990
You told Okya-Wichayen about

169
00:15:20,990 --> 00:15:24,070
what Father and Okya-Kosathibodi discussed,

170
00:15:24,070 --> 00:15:25,060
didn’t you?

171
00:15:28,800 --> 00:15:29,890
Answer me!

172
00:15:31,350 --> 00:15:32,010
Yes.

173
00:15:32,860 --> 00:15:34,260
I told Falcon.

174
00:15:35,200 --> 00:15:36,670
How could you?

175
00:15:36,670 --> 00:15:38,860
You told an outsider about our private affair.

176
00:15:38,860 --> 00:15:41,420
And this involves politics.

177
00:15:41,420 --> 00:15:42,380
It’s unacceptable.

178
00:15:42,750 --> 00:15:43,910
Please hear me out.

179
00:15:44,470 --> 00:15:46,400
Hear your excuses out?

180
00:15:47,030 --> 00:15:48,860
You’ve chosen Okya-Wichayen’s side.

181
00:15:49,090 --> 00:15:50,620
Are you that worried about him,

182
00:15:50,620 --> 00:15:52,240
that you rushed out to see him?

183
00:15:52,700 --> 00:15:53,710
You’ve got it all wrong.

184
00:15:54,610 --> 00:15:55,390
ศet me explain.

185
00:15:55,390 --> 00:15:56,410
I’m not listening!

186
00:15:56,410 --> 00:15:57,970
You’re wrong this time.

187
00:15:58,860 --> 00:16:00,970
If you aren’t going to listen,

188
00:16:01,470 --> 00:16:02,360
then suit yourself.

189
00:16:07,890 --> 00:16:08,940
Whatever.

190
00:16:16,240 --> 00:16:19,350
My master was wrong to eavesdrop and go see Lord Falcon.

191
00:16:20,130 --> 00:16:21,740
But he didn’t say anything.

192
00:16:22,210 --> 00:16:25,250
He only warned Lord Falcon not to overreach himself.

193
00:16:25,540 --> 00:16:26,260
Really?

194
00:16:26,260 --> 00:16:26,900
Yeah.

195
00:16:27,110 --> 00:16:28,340
Go tell Lord Muen

196
00:16:28,700 --> 00:16:30,390
that he misunderstood my master.

197
00:16:34,220 --> 00:16:35,510
-My lord.
-What?

198
00:17:04,800 --> 00:17:05,660
Gaew.

199
00:17:08,579 --> 00:17:10,020
About Okya-Wichayen…

200
00:17:11,089 --> 00:17:12,349
I know the truth now.

201
00:17:14,060 --> 00:17:15,329
I misunderstood you.

202
00:17:17,630 --> 00:17:18,460
I’m sorry.

203
00:17:21,890 --> 00:17:23,359
Have you forgiven me now, P’Muen?

204
00:17:28,150 --> 00:17:29,170
I was wrong too.

205
00:17:30,730 --> 00:17:32,150
I shouldn’t have eavesdropped

206
00:17:32,150 --> 00:17:33,370
or secretly warned Falcon.

207
00:17:35,460 --> 00:17:37,020
And I shouldn’t have treated you like that.

208
00:17:42,060 --> 00:17:42,890
I’m sorry.

209
00:17:52,580 --> 00:17:53,340
Wanna make up?

210
00:17:57,510 --> 00:17:58,340
What’s this?

211
00:18:01,210 --> 00:18:02,070
Hold out your finger.

212
00:18:03,180 --> 00:18:04,010
Your pinky.

213
00:18:11,190 --> 00:18:12,030
Let’s make up.

214
00:18:15,540 --> 00:18:16,310
Say it.

215
00:18:19,040 --> 00:18:19,870
Let’s make up.

216
00:18:20,630 --> 00:18:21,520
And smile.

217
00:18:22,060 --> 00:18:23,250
Don’t look so fierce.

218
00:18:35,820 --> 00:18:37,550
My lord.

219
00:18:40,520 --> 00:18:41,270
Yes?

220
00:18:42,010 --> 00:18:45,600
Master wants you and Gaew to meet him at the central hall.

221
00:18:55,850 --> 00:18:58,860
Okkhun-Phetphakdi, my old friend who lives in Song Khwae,

222
00:18:59,810 --> 00:19:00,930
has fallen seriously ill.

223
00:19:01,600 --> 00:19:04,260
I’ve prepared some medicine,

224
00:19:04,260 --> 00:19:05,920
and I’d like to visit him myself,

225
00:19:05,920 --> 00:19:07,820
but I’m afraid I’ll end up getting sick too,

226
00:19:07,820 --> 00:19:09,010
since it’s such a long journey.

227
00:19:09,350 --> 00:19:13,530
So I’d like Dech and Gaew to visit him

228
00:19:13,870 --> 00:19:16,300
and deliver the medicine on my behalf.

229
00:19:16,820 --> 00:19:18,750
And you’ll get a chance to get to know him.

230
00:19:19,200 --> 00:19:21,980
When would you like Gaew and me to leave?

231
00:19:22,410 --> 00:19:23,370
Today.

232
00:19:28,430 --> 00:19:28,960
Understood.

233
00:19:58,780 --> 00:20:00,990
Jintao, has the agarwood arrived yet?

234
00:20:00,990 --> 00:20:02,140
Not yet.

235
00:20:02,550 --> 00:20:03,980
Let me know as soon as it does.

236
00:20:04,270 --> 00:20:04,960
Yes, sir.

237
00:20:06,940 --> 00:20:08,010
I don’t like this one.

238
00:20:09,580 --> 00:20:11,310
This one just arrived from China.

239
00:20:12,970 --> 00:20:13,980
From China?

240
00:20:20,820 --> 00:20:21,790
What do you think?

241
00:20:23,340 --> 00:20:24,340
I like it.

242
00:20:33,930 --> 00:20:35,100
I got a new wine.

243
00:20:36,170 --> 00:20:37,730
It’s from China. Give it a try.

244
00:20:39,930 --> 00:20:41,730
Thank you, my lord.

245
00:20:55,100 --> 00:20:56,130
Wad?

246
00:20:59,500 --> 00:21:00,200
Wad, wait.

247
00:21:00,630 --> 00:21:01,500
Wad.

248
00:21:02,570 --> 00:21:04,430
It’s not what you think.

249
00:21:12,700 --> 00:21:14,770
I’m just having a drink with my friend.

250
00:21:15,230 --> 00:21:16,930
The courtesan you saw

251
00:21:16,930 --> 00:21:18,170
was with my friend.

252
00:21:19,000 --> 00:21:21,370
I have nothing to do with her.

253
00:21:21,870 --> 00:21:24,230
I was by myself.

254
00:21:25,070 --> 00:21:27,100
Don’t misunderstand me.

255
00:21:28,200 --> 00:21:30,000
It’s not what I thought?

256
00:21:30,570 --> 00:21:32,630
You were drinking with your friend.

257
00:21:33,330 --> 00:21:34,970
And the courtesan I saw

258
00:21:34,970 --> 00:21:36,570
was with your friend.

259
00:21:37,300 --> 00:21:38,170
Is that so?

260
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:40,000
Yes.

261
00:21:41,970 --> 00:21:43,200
Yes, of course.

262
00:21:44,500 --> 00:21:45,630
Reung.

263
00:21:47,400 --> 00:21:50,070
Sometimes you may seem a little boring,

264
00:21:55,030 --> 00:21:56,470
but you’re very patient

265
00:21:57,070 --> 00:21:58,670
and caring.

266
00:22:04,970 --> 00:22:06,130
Yes, of course.

267
00:22:07,330 --> 00:22:09,770
I may seem a little boring,

268
00:22:10,500 --> 00:22:12,400
but I’m very patient

269
00:22:12,400 --> 00:22:14,070
and caring.

270
00:22:15,430 --> 00:22:16,670
Wad.

271
00:22:17,470 --> 00:22:19,770
You seem stubborn,

272
00:22:19,770 --> 00:22:21,030
competitive,

273
00:22:21,600 --> 00:22:23,170
and never care about anyone,

274
00:22:23,800 --> 00:22:25,800
but deep down,

275
00:22:27,530 --> 00:22:30,170
you’re the kindest.

276
00:22:31,970 --> 00:22:33,500
Yes, of course.

277
00:22:34,470 --> 00:22:36,600
I may seem stubborn,

278
00:22:36,600 --> 00:22:37,900
competitive,

279
00:22:38,830 --> 00:22:40,870
and never care about anyone,

280
00:22:41,070 --> 00:22:42,300
but deep down,

281
00:22:42,730 --> 00:22:44,730
I’m the kindest.

282
00:22:55,970 --> 00:22:59,170
What brings you here today?

283
00:22:59,670 --> 00:23:01,830
I’m looking for agarwood,

284
00:23:01,830 --> 00:23:04,730
but none of the herbal shops have it,

285
00:23:07,100 --> 00:23:09,900
Agarwood?

286
00:23:15,000 --> 00:23:16,530
And these Kanom Kong…

287
00:23:17,370 --> 00:23:19,930
You said they have such a beautiful meaning,

288
00:23:20,670 --> 00:23:22,930
symbolizing unwavering love.

289
00:23:26,370 --> 00:23:29,600
Do you want me to give them to Dech?

290
00:23:30,200 --> 00:23:31,470
No.

291
00:23:31,470 --> 00:23:33,870
I bought them for you.

292
00:23:53,600 --> 00:23:54,970
Actually,

293
00:23:54,970 --> 00:23:57,170
I thought you’d be at the police department.

294
00:23:57,670 --> 00:23:59,470
I’m glad I found you here.

295
00:24:00,930 --> 00:24:02,200
I’ll be going now.

296
00:24:27,230 --> 00:24:28,130
Jintao.

297
00:24:28,470 --> 00:24:29,530
Yes, sir.

298
00:24:30,400 --> 00:24:32,000
If the agarwood arrives,

299
00:24:33,200 --> 00:24:34,600
don’t sell it to Wad.

300
00:24:36,270 --> 00:24:37,330
Sell it to me.

301
00:24:38,370 --> 00:24:39,530
Yes, sir.

302
00:25:20,530 --> 00:25:22,000
Are you feeling unwell?

303
00:25:22,730 --> 00:25:24,400
It’s probably because of the cold weather.

304
00:25:34,030 --> 00:25:35,800
Song Khwae is still a long way off.

305
00:25:36,230 --> 00:25:37,700
It’ll be dark before we get there.

306
00:25:40,830 --> 00:25:42,470
Let’s find a place to rest first.

307
00:26:52,430 --> 00:26:54,030
You’re burning up.

308
00:26:55,100 --> 00:26:56,600
You have a fever.

309
00:27:01,900 --> 00:27:03,770
I think you’re right.

310
00:27:26,270 --> 00:27:28,330
The medicine for Father’s friend

311
00:27:28,830 --> 00:27:30,220
is good for bringing down a fever.

312
00:27:30,970 --> 00:27:32,220
My mother used to give it to me.

313
00:27:58,600 --> 00:27:59,900
Is it bitter?

314
00:28:02,570 --> 00:28:03,700
It is.

315
00:28:06,630 --> 00:28:07,870
A good medicine

316
00:28:08,400 --> 00:28:09,500
tastes bitter.

317
00:30:29,300 --> 00:30:31,030
Wait, P’Muen.

318
00:30:36,270 --> 00:30:37,600
You…

319
00:30:37,600 --> 00:30:39,030
don’t want this?

320
00:30:40,970 --> 00:30:42,770
I do.

321
00:30:46,430 --> 00:30:48,530
But not now.

322
00:30:50,570 --> 00:30:52,970
I don’t want you to catch my fever.

323
00:30:53,900 --> 00:30:55,570
If you get sick,

324
00:30:56,670 --> 00:30:58,300
who’s going to take care of me?

325
00:31:14,070 --> 00:31:16,170
I just want your fever to go away.

326
00:31:18,470 --> 00:31:20,070
How?

327
00:31:49,170 --> 00:31:51,000
Will this really...

328
00:31:51,000 --> 00:31:53,530
make my fever go away, P’Muen?

329
00:31:57,730 --> 00:31:58,870
Yes.

330
00:31:59,770 --> 00:32:01,370
Trust me.

331
00:32:34,000 --> 00:32:36,030
How old is Wad now?

332
00:32:36,770 --> 00:32:38,900
He’ll be 20 this year, my lord.

333
00:32:39,370 --> 00:32:41,900
It’s about time he found a wife.

334
00:32:42,530 --> 00:32:43,530
Hm.

335
00:32:43,770 --> 00:32:44,830
Lord Chaopraya,

336
00:32:44,830 --> 00:32:46,470
you have a daughter, right?

337
00:32:47,200 --> 00:32:48,430
Yes.

338
00:32:48,430 --> 00:32:50,470
She’s four years younger than Wad.

339
00:32:52,030 --> 00:32:52,900
Well,

340
00:32:52,900 --> 00:32:54,100
wonderful.

341
00:32:54,630 --> 00:32:55,470
Then,

342
00:32:55,470 --> 00:32:56,830
shall we let them meet

343
00:32:57,170 --> 00:32:58,470
and get to know each other?

344
00:32:59,170 --> 00:33:00,770
Maybe our families

345
00:33:01,230 --> 00:33:02,670
can become one.

346
00:33:02,670 --> 00:33:03,930
What do you think?

347
00:33:04,670 --> 00:33:06,300
Good idea, Lord Okya.

348
00:33:07,870 --> 00:33:09,100
When you have time,

349
00:33:09,100 --> 00:33:10,870
come have a meal at my home.

350
00:33:24,630 --> 00:33:25,870
Let’s go.

351
00:33:27,730 --> 00:33:29,170
Did you hear

352
00:33:29,170 --> 00:33:31,100
what I just said?

353
00:33:31,500 --> 00:33:32,900
Yes, Father.

354
00:33:34,700 --> 00:33:37,200
It’s time for you to find a wife,

355
00:33:37,200 --> 00:33:38,300
Wad.

356
00:33:40,930 --> 00:33:42,570
Marriage

357
00:33:42,570 --> 00:33:44,430
isn’t about two people.

358
00:33:45,370 --> 00:33:47,530
It’s the union of two families.

359
00:33:49,000 --> 00:33:51,000
I haven’t thought about it yet.

360
00:33:51,930 --> 00:33:53,130
Why not?

361
00:33:54,670 --> 00:33:55,670
Oh.

362
00:33:55,670 --> 00:33:56,730
Or perhaps…

363
00:33:57,370 --> 00:33:59,070
Do you already have someone in mind?

364
00:33:59,430 --> 00:34:00,370
Well?

365
00:34:00,370 --> 00:34:01,730
Who is she?

366
00:34:01,730 --> 00:34:03,000
Tell me.

367
00:34:04,800 --> 00:34:06,500
I’ll tell you

368
00:34:07,070 --> 00:34:08,699
when I’m more certain.

369
00:34:09,730 --> 00:34:11,630
If you already like someone,

370
00:34:11,630 --> 00:34:13,300
I’m happy for you.

371
00:34:31,170 --> 00:34:33,600
Lord Okkhun sent you these gifts.

372
00:34:33,600 --> 00:34:34,230
Hm.

373
00:34:34,230 --> 00:34:35,570
Thank you.

374
00:34:42,900 --> 00:34:44,570
Are you making krathongs?

375
00:34:45,170 --> 00:34:46,130
Yes.

376
00:34:46,130 --> 00:34:49,330
Tonight is the full moon of the twelfth lunar month.

377
00:34:57,930 --> 00:34:59,070
Let me help.

378
00:35:09,070 --> 00:35:10,530
Is it already Loy Krathong day?

379
00:35:11,070 --> 00:35:12,470
Great.

380
00:35:12,470 --> 00:35:14,200
How long have you been here?

381
00:35:16,570 --> 00:35:18,430
I wonder how Grandma’s doing.

382
00:35:19,300 --> 00:35:20,570
I miss her so much.

383
00:35:40,730 --> 00:35:42,000
Do you already

384
00:35:42,370 --> 00:35:44,630
have someone in mind?

385
00:35:44,630 --> 00:35:45,570
Well?

386
00:35:45,570 --> 00:35:48,200
Who is she? Tell me.

387
00:35:49,970 --> 00:35:51,870
I’ll tell you

388
00:35:52,200 --> 00:35:53,930
when I’m more certain.

389
00:36:10,030 --> 00:36:11,030
Wad.

390
00:36:13,130 --> 00:36:14,130
Over here.

391
00:36:16,870 --> 00:36:18,100
Reung.

392
00:36:21,300 --> 00:36:23,070
Why are you here?

393
00:36:23,830 --> 00:36:25,600
I want to float krathong with you.

394
00:36:29,330 --> 00:36:31,170
I couldn’t come through the front gate,

395
00:36:31,670 --> 00:36:33,600
or Lord Okya would see me.

396
00:36:33,600 --> 00:36:35,170
Father isn’t home.

397
00:36:39,300 --> 00:36:41,200
Then what are we waiting for?

398
00:36:45,170 --> 00:36:47,000
Come float a krathong with me.

399
00:36:48,770 --> 00:36:50,330
Float a krathong?

400
00:36:50,330 --> 00:36:51,700
In the water?

401
00:37:48,200 --> 00:37:49,770
Reung.

402
00:37:50,730 --> 00:37:52,930
Do you like me?

403
00:37:58,430 --> 00:37:59,930
Yes, of course.

404
00:38:00,900 --> 00:38:02,800
I like you,

405
00:38:04,770 --> 00:38:05,770
Wad.

406
00:39:50,600 --> 00:39:52,870
Lord Phra Sriprach has arrived.

407
00:40:04,230 --> 00:40:06,770
Thank you for granting me an audience.

408
00:40:19,770 --> 00:40:20,770
Lady Thao,

409
00:40:21,530 --> 00:40:23,030
wait for me at the pier.

410
00:40:23,170 --> 00:40:24,330
Yes, Your Highness.

411
00:40:31,700 --> 00:40:33,270
Everything…

412
00:40:34,270 --> 00:40:35,930
was my fault.

413
00:40:36,870 --> 00:40:38,670
I beg your forgiveness

414
00:40:39,000 --> 00:40:40,570
for not knowing my place,

415
00:40:41,030 --> 00:40:43,570
daring to dream beyond my station.

416
00:40:48,630 --> 00:40:50,500
The reason I asked you to come…

417
00:40:52,130 --> 00:40:54,130
was to return this.

418
00:41:09,800 --> 00:41:12,550
The first poem you wrote for me.

419
00:41:24,370 --> 00:41:25,500
Love.

420
00:41:27,600 --> 00:41:29,700
Love at first sight.

421
00:41:30,430 --> 00:41:31,770
From the moment

422
00:41:32,670 --> 00:41:33,900
our eyes met,

423
00:41:34,570 --> 00:41:36,470
my heart skipped a beat.

424
00:41:37,030 --> 00:41:38,100
The feeling

425
00:41:40,470 --> 00:41:41,530
could no longer

426
00:41:42,330 --> 00:41:44,070
be hidden.

427
00:41:44,570 --> 00:41:46,870
My heart

428
00:41:48,470 --> 00:41:49,570
kept calling out

429
00:41:50,200 --> 00:41:52,370
to you.

430
00:41:55,370 --> 00:41:57,170
It belongs to you.

431
00:42:08,770 --> 00:42:09,770
Your Highness.

432
00:42:13,300 --> 00:42:14,470
Lord Phra Sriprach.

433
00:42:22,570 --> 00:42:24,330
This is a dok kaew krathong.

434
00:42:25,830 --> 00:42:27,130
A dok kaew flower?

435
00:42:27,130 --> 00:42:28,930
You named it after me?

436
00:42:30,900 --> 00:42:32,830
You could say that.

437
00:42:35,000 --> 00:42:36,100
Let’s make a wish.

438
00:43:26,370 --> 00:43:27,900
Do you know…

439
00:43:28,700 --> 00:43:30,600
what I wished for?

440
00:43:32,700 --> 00:43:34,400
How could I know?

441
00:43:36,330 --> 00:43:38,070
I wished that…

442
00:43:39,070 --> 00:43:40,370
next year…

443
00:43:41,270 --> 00:43:43,100
we’ll get to float a krathong together again.

444
00:43:48,400 --> 00:43:50,100
Why are you so quiet?

445
00:43:58,930 --> 00:44:00,000
I promise.

446
00:44:02,270 --> 00:44:04,230
If I’m still here,

447
00:44:05,570 --> 00:44:08,570
I’ll float a krathong with you every year.

448
00:44:08,570 --> 00:44:10,130
Confirm.

449
00:44:12,400 --> 00:44:14,330
What does confirm mean?

450
00:44:15,830 --> 00:44:17,400
It means a firm promise.

451
00:44:23,030 --> 00:44:24,000
Here.

452
00:44:30,270 --> 00:44:32,170
I wrote you a poem.

453
00:44:32,970 --> 00:44:34,070
Wow.

454
00:44:39,000 --> 00:44:40,500
What is love?

455
00:44:40,500 --> 00:44:41,930
And to love?

456
00:44:41,930 --> 00:44:43,300
I never knew.

457
00:44:44,370 --> 00:44:45,700
Until I saw you,

458
00:44:45,700 --> 00:44:46,970
I know without a doubt

459
00:44:46,970 --> 00:44:48,300
that love was you.

460
00:44:49,130 --> 00:44:50,270
When we're apart,

461
00:44:50,270 --> 00:44:51,630
my heart can't stay

462
00:44:51,630 --> 00:44:52,900
without you.

463
00:44:53,970 --> 00:44:55,130
Eventually,

464
00:44:55,130 --> 00:44:56,100
my heart always

465
00:44:56,100 --> 00:44:57,600
drifts back to you.

466
00:44:58,030 --> 00:44:59,130
Guided by fate,

467
00:44:59,130 --> 00:45:00,200
our paths

468
00:45:00,200 --> 00:45:01,530
have crossed.

469
00:45:02,430 --> 00:45:03,500
Our hearts

470
00:45:03,500 --> 00:45:04,800
have become one,

471
00:45:04,800 --> 00:45:05,970
overflowing with love.

472
00:45:06,600 --> 00:45:07,630
The names

473
00:45:07,630 --> 00:45:09,130
Dech and Gaew

474
00:45:09,130 --> 00:45:10,970
are more than names.

475
00:45:11,770 --> 00:45:13,130
If fate is kind,

476
00:45:13,430 --> 00:45:14,800
may I love you

477
00:45:15,170 --> 00:45:16,770
through every lifetime.

478
00:46:00,200 --> 00:46:01,570
Falcon?

479
00:46:03,630 --> 00:46:04,370
P’Muen.

480
00:46:04,370 --> 00:46:05,700
Wait here a moment.

481
00:46:17,500 --> 00:46:20,900
We have over 800 soldiers.

482
00:46:21,270 --> 00:46:24,200
That should be enough for your great plan.

483
00:46:26,000 --> 00:46:27,000
Yes.

484
00:46:27,770 --> 00:46:32,330
It should be enough to take on Prince Chao Fa Aphai Thot

485
00:46:32,330 --> 00:46:34,730
and Lord Phra Phetracha’s faction.

486
00:46:35,870 --> 00:46:40,970
Right now, His Majesty completely trusts me,

487
00:46:42,900 --> 00:46:50,300
making them resentful, so our plan should be carried out soon.

488
00:46:51,030 --> 00:46:52,270
Are you certain?

489
00:46:53,400 --> 00:46:54,870
If they are going to destroy me,

490
00:46:55,870 --> 00:46:59,200
I’ll destroy them first.

491
00:46:59,200 --> 00:47:03,770
You know how much the Siamese nobles hate me.

492
00:47:05,530 --> 00:47:06,970
In that case,

493
00:47:06,970 --> 00:47:10,770
I’ll leave 50 soldiers here to protect you,

494
00:47:10,770 --> 00:47:13,430
then I’ll return to the Bangkok fortress.

495
00:47:13,930 --> 00:47:16,330
If there’s anything urgent,

496
00:47:16,330 --> 00:47:19,830
send me a messenger.

497
00:47:20,200 --> 00:47:21,730
Thank you very much.

498
00:47:41,300 --> 00:47:42,470
Let’s talk somewhere else.

499
00:47:42,470 --> 00:47:43,630
Alright.

500
00:47:54,770 --> 00:47:56,070
Falcon is planning something dangerous.

501
00:47:56,070 --> 00:47:56,970
I have to stop him.

502
00:47:57,470 --> 00:47:58,770
Gaew.

503
00:47:59,300 --> 00:48:00,500
What are you doing?

504
00:48:01,600 --> 00:48:02,930
Do you know

505
00:48:03,470 --> 00:48:04,800
this is getting out of hand?

506
00:48:07,130 --> 00:48:08,370
I’m going to stop Falcon.

507
00:48:12,200 --> 00:48:13,330
P’Muen!

508
00:48:13,830 --> 00:48:15,030
What are you doing?

509
00:48:15,430 --> 00:48:16,730
Put it down!

510
00:48:17,000 --> 00:48:18,600
Promise me…

511
00:48:19,470 --> 00:48:21,400
you won’t do anything dangerous.

512
00:48:23,300 --> 00:48:24,630
Promise me.

513
00:48:27,970 --> 00:48:29,730
Promise me, Gaew.

514
00:48:32,230 --> 00:48:33,470
I promise.

515
00:48:33,800 --> 00:48:35,200
I promise.

516
00:48:35,730 --> 00:48:38,170
Please put the dagger down. Don’t do this.

517
00:48:48,270 --> 00:48:49,970
If anything happens to you,

518
00:48:52,930 --> 00:48:55,230
I won’t be able to live anymore.

519
00:48:57,170 --> 00:48:58,400
P’Muen.

520
00:49:12,130 --> 00:49:13,700
My lord!

521
00:49:15,470 --> 00:49:16,630
This is bad.

522
00:49:16,630 --> 00:49:17,870
What happened?

523
00:49:18,200 --> 00:49:19,400
Lord Phra Sriprach

524
00:49:19,730 --> 00:49:20,970
has been arrested.

525
00:49:24,370 --> 00:49:25,800
P’Sri.

526
00:49:58,700 --> 00:50:00,900
I have no choice.

527
00:50:02,100 --> 00:50:03,710
Now that we’re by the sea,

528
00:50:03,710 --> 00:50:07,130
do you know how to ride the waves?

529
00:50:07,400 --> 00:50:09,030
Ride the waves?

530
00:50:09,630 --> 00:50:11,170
What does that mean, P’Muen?

531
00:50:11,970 --> 00:50:14,400
That spell must have brought me here.

532
00:50:14,400 --> 00:50:16,400
If P’Khun performs the ritual again,

533
00:50:16,400 --> 00:50:18,330
will I be able to go home?

534
00:50:19,100 --> 00:50:21,400
The English weapons trade records.

535
00:50:23,270 --> 00:50:24,370
Stop!
